BRepBlend_SurfRstLineBuilder::InternalPerform: when the contact of a blend
rolling on a restriction (an edge) leaves the surface across one of its arcs
in the same step as the point on the restriction leaves the restriction's
domain (Blend_OnRst12, e.g. both reach a face at the end at once), the
solution took the parameter on the surface's arc (solinvs(3)) as the
parameter on the restriction, and the extremity on the surface took the
guide's parameter (solinvs(1)) as the parameter on the arc. The section
then jumped, TestArret rejected it and the walk ended short of both arcs.
The vector of the inverse function Blend_SurfCurvFuncInv is (guide,
restriction, arc): the restriction's parameter is solinvs(2) and the arc's
solinvs(3), as the Blend_OnRst1 case and PerformFirstSection use them.
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_SurfRstLineBuilder.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_SurfRstLineBuilder.cxx
index 7b05208..5f06577 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_SurfRstLineBuilder.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_SurfRstLineBuilder.cxx
@@ -734,7 +734,9 @@ void BRepBlend_SurfRstLineBuilder::InternalPerform(Blend_SurfRstFunction&  Func,
             param  = 0.5 * (ws + wrst);
             sol(1) = U;
             sol(2) = V;
-            sol(3) = solinvs(3);
+            // the parameter on the restriction, as for Blend_OnRst1
+            // (solinvs: guide, restriction, arc of the surface)
+            sol(3) = solinvs(2);
           }
           else if (sens * (ws - wrst) < 0)
           {
@@ -955,7 +957,7 @@ void BRepBlend_SurfRstLineBuilder::InternalPerform(Blend_SurfRstFunction&  Func,
         {
           line->Prepend(previousP);
         }
-        MakeExtremity(Exts, true, Arc, solinvs(1), IsVtxs, Vtxs);
+        MakeExtremity(Exts, true, Arc, solinvs(3), IsVtxs, Vtxs);
         MakeExtremity(Extrst, false, rst, sol(3), IsVtxrst, Vtxrst);
         Arrive = true;
       }
